 ],
 "render_tail_analysis": "Combat intervals over 33 ms rose from a median of 2 to 3 per run of 730-970 combat frames (baseline 1-3, candidate 3-5). Per-phase costs did not: native layout/paint/present means and p99s, Ruby update p95/p99 and the count of native frames over 16 ms were equal or lower in the candidate. The extra intervals are single dropped frames (34-41 ms) where two on-time Ruby updates straddle a 20-24 ms native frame; such frames occur in both arms. Craters now arrive about 230 ms sooner after a blast, so their tile loads overlap the blast's busiest frames; this is the most likely explanation but was not isolated. Off-CPU stalls (wall far above CPU) occurred in both arms and failed the 60 ms budget in 3 of 10 runs (baseline 1, candidate 2).",
 "checks": {
